## Notes (not defects)
1. `check_p2.py` `L14.world1-end-screen` expected the World 1 clear screen after the 1-4 Toad; since round 2 the Toad leads to 2-1. I changed the check to `L14.toad-leads-to-2-1` (this is the brief's intended behaviour).
2. The developer's exclusion of "hard-mode" objects (e.g. 2-3's Koopas/Paratroopas) is faithful: in the disassembly the enemy second-byte bit 6 means hard mode only, which is enabled from 5-3 on.
3. Swimming has no friction (the code says "NES values"); consistent with the original.
4. `#level=` is read once at start, so after game over or the clear screen a restart goes back to the hash level. It is a debug feature; no effect without a hash.
5. 2-1 starts next to a large castle: matches the original map.
6. Bot leads, not defects: the "fair" bot stalls in 2-1 (dies in the pit at column 107-113 and next to the pipe Piranha at column 115) and 2-3 (pit at x=2020); the search bot ignores enemies and falls in the coin-heaven pit in 2-1 (falling returns you to the level, so its "every macro dies" is its own limit). A human play of those spots is for the playtester.

## Not covered
Music and sound by ear (only that the right track/sfx is requested), real-keyboard feel, pixel-level fidelity to the original, and a complete real-play (no god mode, no teleport) swim of 2-2 with all enemies; the simple swim bot got stuck at x=1620 and I did not take it further. The playtester's play of 2-2 is the open evidence there.

